{"id": "EUVD-2026-103845", "enisaUuid": "6b4d689d-6fa7-3adc-8a8f-73b3575c870c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: typec: tipd: fix uninitialized typec_partner_desc in tps6598x_connect()\n\ntps6598x_connect() passes a stack-allocated typec_partner_desc to\ntypec_register_partner() after initializing only usb_pd, accessory and\nidentity.\n\ntypec_register_partner() copies attach and deattach from the descriptor\ninto the partner. With those fields left unset, garbage function pointers\nmay be stored and later invoked from typec_partner_link_device() when a USB\ndevice is linked to the port. Uninitialized pd_revision and usb_capability\nsimilarly leak stack data through partner sysfs.\n\nZero-initialize the descriptor so optional callbacks remain NULL and the\nremaining fields are zero.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:47:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:56:34", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a39d53f70e637ff3970046c32106a0e64fca62cd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4b6823ce0e548491cb9663303cba28e18d351096", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/282be6ae8be791762740107c79cecf5121f66063", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dac0c073c6ad5f1bbb5e9fea9023fc1b4dab5e14", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c4b27b3605788bbf9e4251f3cd4ab94645ab036f"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f983-5vc9-m6xh", "CVE-2026-98760"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "31acba0f-8c1e-37b6-b82d-caccf03db6d5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "385a00cd-6239-35db-98ea-9016dae30277", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "49d2c6fc-5098-39b7-8b20-ef09a878d99b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0a4c005bd1715d8b32a368ed5516a6ee7e603d18 <282be6ae8be791762740107c79cecf5121f66063"}, {"id": "4b2ede34-8d81-3090-a4b2-b10269c107df", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0a4c005bd1715d8b32a368ed5516a6ee7e603d18 <a39d53f70e637ff3970046c32106a0e64fca62cd"}, {"id": "4d8ba5a7-f441-320a-9289-c31279501b98", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0a4c005bd1715d8b32a368ed5516a6ee7e603d18 <c4b27b3605788bbf9e4251f3cd4ab94645ab036f"}, {"id": "6c4e641e-eb55-3528-af1f-4ee1629882a5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0a4c005bd1715d8b32a368ed5516a6ee7e603d18 <4b6823ce0e548491cb9663303cba28e18d351096"}, {"id": "a2d9dc6f-dddb-36ea-8e7b-312a8896f597", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "ab7d1a68-af2f-374c-af8e-2e1455967dc7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "cb11679d-7058-373b-be14-d285844d68e0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.15"}, {"id": "d4e2c7e7-e2f7-34dc-87a2-23693bbe88de", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0a4c005bd1715d8b32a368ed5516a6ee7e603d18 <dac0c073c6ad5f1bbb5e9fea9023fc1b4dab5e14"}, {"id": "da1afd68-8e02-3eed-908c-5275f0379c7f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "e3cc5098-fe1c-363f-b2d5-f5e4d1257151", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e4eb0ab0-051d-38ec-978a-5c6751a77064", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}